albor provides C++ targets for the declarative UI framework:

    find_package(albor CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE albor)          # recommended GPU runtime (Metal / Direct3D)

The portable CPU renderer and the skia reference arrive through the package features
(`albor[blend2d]`, `albor[skia-reference]`):

    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE albor-blend2d)  # the blend2d feature's umbrella

Compile a .ui component at build time:

    albor_build_ui_component(main "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/panel.ui")

Exactly one platform adapter, one text engine and one renderer may be linked; the umbrella
target carries them all, and the granular albor-*-auto targets are the expert surface.

On Windows the consumer's configuration must match the installed binaries' MSVC runtime,
which vcpkg's own consumption provides automatically (both debug and release are built);
a plain-prefix consumer links release at the minimum.

On macOS the deployment floor is 13.3: export MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET before configuring,
or set VCPKG_OSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET in the triplet you build the package with.
